          <td>sRGB</td>
          <td>Standard sRGB (avoid CMYK print profiles)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Understanding the 16:9 Aspect Ratio</h3>
  <p>
    Aspect ratio defines the proportional relationship between image width and height. A 16:9 ratio means that for every 16 units of horizontal width, there are 9 units of vertical height. Because YouTube's video player uses a native 16:9 format, sizing your <strong>YouTube thumbnail dimensions</strong> to 16:9 guarantees that your artwork completely fills the frame without awkward borders.
  </p>

  <h3>Cross-Platform Display Rendering</h3>
  <p>
    Thumbnails must render clearly across diverse viewing environments:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mobile Devices:</strong> Over 70% of YouTube viewing occurs on mobile phones. On small screens, fine details and subtle text disappear, making bold visual elements essential.</li>
    <li><strong>Desktop Browsers:</strong> On computers, thumbnails appear in video grids and compact sidebar preview cards in the suggested feed.</li>
    <li><strong>Connected Smart TVs:</strong> On large 4K and 1080p television screens, low-resolution uploads reveal noticeable blur, pixelation, and artifacts.</li>
  </ul>

