  </p>

  <h3>Common Issues with Unoptimized Images</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Unwanted Letterboxing:</strong> Square (1:1) or standard (4:3) images create black bars on the sides, reducing your usable visual area.</li>
    <li><strong>Upscaling Blur:</strong> Uploading low-resolution graphics forces YouTube to stretch the file, causing soft text and muddy details.</li>
    <li><strong>File Size Rejections:</strong> High-resolution camera files often exceed 5 MB, triggering immediate upload rejections in YouTube Studio.</li>
    <li><strong>Distorted Proportions:</strong> Basic resizing tools sometimes stretch images unevenly, deforming subjects and logos.</li>
  </ul>

