  <h2 id="section-9">9. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>
  <p>
    Here are quick answers to the most common questions regarding YouTube thumbnail dimensions and optimization:
  </p>

  <div class="faq-group">
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-question">What is the recommended YouTube thumbnail size?</h3>
      <p class="faq-answer">
        The official recommended YouTube thumbnail size is <strong>1280 × 720 pixels</strong> with a <strong>16:9 aspect ratio</strong> and a minimum width of 640 pixels. File sizes should remain under 2 MB in JPG, PNG, WebP, or static GIF format.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-question">Can I use 1920 × 1080 pixels for my YouTube thumbnail?</h3>
      <p class="faq-answer">
        Yes. 1920 × 1080 pixels shares the exact same 16:9 aspect ratio as 1280 × 720 pixels. As long as your exported file is under 2 MB, YouTube will accept it smoothly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-question">Why does my YouTube thumbnail look blurry after uploading?</h3>
      <p class="faq-answer">
        Blurriness occurs when you upload an image with dimensions below 1280 × 720 pixels that YouTube stretches to fill larger screen containers. Using a dedicated <a href={toolUrl}>YouTube Thumbnail Resizer</a> ensures your image matches native resolution with crisp clarity.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-question">Is PNG or JPG better for YouTube thumbnails?</h3>
      <p class="faq-answer">
        PNG is preferable for graphics featuring bold typography, sharp logos, and illustrations due to lossless compression. JPG is better for complex photography and portraits to ensure the file remains under 2 MB.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-question">Why is the bottom-right corner of my thumbnail covered?</h3>
      <p class="faq-answer">
        YouTube overlays the video duration timestamp badge in the bottom-right corner of every thumbnail. Keep this area clear of text, faces, or essential graphics.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-question">How do I resize an image for a YouTube thumbnail for free?</h3>
