      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-question">What is considered a good Click-Through Rate (CTR) on YouTube?</h3>
      <p class="faq-answer">
        Average CTR across YouTube generally ranges between 2% and 10%. A CTR above 6% to 8% is typically strong, while standout videos often exceed 10% to 12% in their initial launch phase.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-question">What should I do if my thumbnail file exceeds 2 MB?</h3>
      <p class="faq-answer">
        If your image file is larger than 2 MB, YouTube Studio will reject it. Running the file through an image resizer and compressor reduces the payload while maintaining crisp visual fidelity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

